.Dd April 19, 2026
.Dt CMI_DEBUG 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cmi_debug
.Nd CMI process debug protection service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "kldload cmi"
.Cd "kldload cmi_debug"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
service protects a program from
.Xr ptrace 2
and unauthorized signals using the MACF framework.
.Pp
Protection is scoped by the program nonce: all processes sharing the
same nonce (the calling process and its unexec'd fork descendants) are
shielded.
SIGKILL and SIGCONT are always allowed through the shield.
.Pp
All operations use
.Dv CMI_CALL
(synchronous).
.Ss Operations
.Bl -tag -width DEBUG_OP_ACTIVATE
.It Dv DEBUG_OP_SHIELD
Shield the calling program.
Closing the shield fd removes protection.
.It Dv DEBUG_OP_MINT
Create a debug token (returned as a reply fd).
Only available on an active shield instance.
.It Dv DEBUG_OP_ACTIVATE
Called on a debug token fd.
Authorizes the calling program to ptrace/signal the shielded target.
.El
.Ss Wire protocol
.Bd -literal
#include <cmi_debug_proto.h>

struct debug_request {
    uint32_t op;
    uint32_t _reserved;
};
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cmi 4 ,
.Xr ptrace 2 ,
.Xr mac 4
